# Replace HWID License with Supabase Email/Password Login

## Background

FastSora v1.2.8/1.2.9 uses a HWID-based license system that calls [auth_client.exe](file:///D:/sorabatchcreatevideo-1.1.0-setup/fastsora-1.2.9-setup/$PLUGINSDIR/resources/auth_client.exe) and verifies signatures.
**Goal:** Replace this with Supabase email/password authentication using REST API (to avoid [asar](file:///D:/sorabatchcreatevideo-1.1.0-setup/fastsora-1.2.9-setup/$PLUGINSDIR/resources/app.asar) module loading issues).

## Implementation Status

### Main Process ([out/main/_index.js](file:///D:/sorabatchcreatevideo-1.1.0-setup/fastsora-1.2.9-setup/$PLUGINSDIR/app-extracted/resources/app-unpacked/out/main/_index.js))

#### [COMPLETED] REST API Implementation
Instead of `@supabase/supabase-js`, we use [fetch](file:///D:/sorabatchcreatevideo-1.1.0-setup/fastsora-1.2.8-setup/$PLUGINSDIR/app-64-extracted/resources/app-unpacked/out/renderer/assets/index-Bl7VuV8J.js#28491-28539) to interact with Supabase Auth API:
- [signInWithPassword](file:///D:/sorabatchcreatevideo-1.1.0-setup/fastsora-1.2.9-setup/$PLUGINSDIR/app-extracted/resources/app-unpacked/out/main/_index.js#4430-4449): POST `/auth/v1/token?grant_type=password`
- [getProfile](file:///D:/sorabatchcreatevideo-1.1.0-setup/fastsora-1.2.8-setup/$PLUGINSDIR/app-64-extracted/resources/app-unpacked/out/main/_index.js#81-92): GET `/rest/v1/profiles`
- [checkSession](file:///D:/sorabatchcreatevideo-1.1.0-setup/fastsora-1.2.9-setup/$PLUGINSDIR/app-extracted/resources/app-unpacked/out/preload/index.js#22-23): In-memory session check + [getUser](file:///D:/sorabatchcreatevideo-1.1.0-setup/fastsora-1.2.8-setup/$PLUGINSDIR/app-64-extracted/resources/app-unpacked/out/preload/index.js#80-81) if needed.

#### [COMPLETED] License Bypass
- Added `days: 99999` to [login](file:///D:/sorabatchcreatevideo-1.1.0-setup/fastsora-1.2.8-setup/$PLUGINSDIR/app-64-extracted/resources/app-unpacked/out/preload/index.js#14-16) and [checkSession](file:///D:/sorabatchcreatevideo-1.1.0-setup/fastsora-1.2.9-setup/$PLUGINSDIR/app-extracted/resources/app-unpacked/out/preload/index.js#22-23) responses.
- This forces the renderer to display "Lifetime" license.

### Renderer/Vue UI Changes

